A||N||5||FIERO1985||NEED INFO ON OIL PAN REMOVAL V6||||1||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||04-24-2001||05:31 PM||||I am going to take off my oil pan completely tommarow to fix a bad seal when I did the timing chain job! I got the starter off and the flywheel dust shield all the bolts out but the pan is hanging there because the motor mount. I know you must jack the motor up. Can you guys give me some info on how to complete this job? please put in steps(where to jack, how high, things like that!)<P><BR>Thanks <BR>Dan<BR><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||07:28 PM||||hey, do you live up on rt 62. Ive seen a few Fieros parked in a yard north of new albany.||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||04-24-2001||11:40 PM||||Check out some archives their are plenty of<BR>post on this subject, only the headliner<BR>problems may have more post.Its all in the<BR>archives GOOD LUCK!||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnmac||04-25-2001||03:43 AM||||It is a *****  of job. I did mine a couple of months ago.<P>Steps to do:<P>Support alternator bracket side engine with small hydraulic jack sitting on suspension A frame. Raise about 3 inches.<P>Remove engine support bracket.<P>I also had to lower my exhaust system.<P>I used plenty of permatex high temp gasket seal when I placed the pan back on.<P>My engine had 100,000 miles on it. First time pan was removed and don't plan to do it again.<P>Pontiac engineers - garbage design.<P>Hope this helps.<P>John MacHaffie<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||04-25-2001||09:01 AM||||It's quite simple:<P>Remove the nuts from the studs in the engine mount, and loosen the bolts that hold the engine mount bracket to the engine. Once that's done, put your jack under the pan and jack the engine up enough to get the engine mount out and the engine mount bracket off. You can put a 2x4 block between the cradle rail and the crank pulley to support the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIERO1985||04-28-2001||02:52 PM||||thanks, and no I am not off of 62 but I think I know who you are talking about!<P>thanks again<BR>Dan<BR>||||reg||1
